    "text": "This is a greedy heuristic, not a proven-optimal solver. Each step takes the vehicle that becomes free earliest and gives it the unassigned ride with the best points-per-time-consumed ratio that it can still finish by its deadline. Rides a vehicle cannot complete are skipped, and a vehicle with no feasible ride is retired. The work is roughly O(N\u00b2) in the worst case, well within the time limit for N \u2264 10000. I have not compiled or run it against real data sets.\n\n```cpp\n#include <bits/stdc++.h>\nusing namespace std;\n\nint main() {\n    ios::sync_with_stdio(false);\n    cin.tie(nullptr);\n\n    long long R, C, F, N, B, T;\n    cin >> R >> C >> F >> N >> B >> T;\n\n    vector<long long> a(N), b(N), x(N), y(N), s(N), f(N), d(N);\n    for (int i = 0; i < N; ++i) {\n        cin >> a[i] >> b[i] >> x[i] >> y[i] >> s[i] >> f[i];\n        d[i] = llabs(x[i] - a[i]) + llabs(y[i] - b[i]);\n    }\n\n    // Vehicle state\n    vector<long long> pr(F, 0), pc(F, 0), tf(F, 0);\n    vector<char> active(F, 1);\n    vector<vector<int>> plan(F);\n\n    // Candidate rides (unassigned), kept in a vector with swap-remove\n    vector<int> cand(N);\n    for (int i = 0; i < N; ++i) cand[i] = i;\n\n    while (true) {\n        // Pick the active vehicle that is free earliest (ties: lower index)\n        int v = -1;\n        for (int i = 0; i < F; ++i) {\n            if (!active[i]) continue;\n            if (v == -1 || tf[i] < tf[v]) v = i;\n        }\n        if (v == -1 || cand.empty()) break;\n\n        long long t = tf[v];\n        double bestVal = -1.0;\n        int bestIdx = -1;          // index into cand\n        long long bestEnd = 0;\n\n        for (int k = 0; k < (int)cand.size(); ++k) {\n            int r = cand[k];\n            long long ds = llabs(pr[v] - a[r]) + llabs(pc[v] - b[r]);\n            long long ts = max(t + ds, s[r]);\n            long long end = ts + d[r];\n            if (end > f[r]) continue;\n            long long pts = d[r] + (ts == s[r] ? B : 0);\n            double val = (double)pts / (double)(end - t);\n            if (val > bestVal) {\n                bestVal = val;\n                bestIdx = k;\n                bestEnd = end;\n            }\n        }\n\n        if (bestIdx == -1) {\n            // No feasible ride for this vehicle any more\n            active[v] = 0;\n            continue;\n        }\n\n        int r = cand[bestIdx];\n        plan[v].push_back(r);\n        tf[v] = bestEnd;\n        pr[v] = x[r];\n        pc[v] = y[r];\n\n        cand[bestIdx] = cand.back();\n        cand.pop_back();\n    }\n\n    string out;\n    out.reserve(1 << 20);\n    for (int i = 0; i < F; ++i) {\n        out += to_string(plan[i].size());\n        for (int r : plan[i]) {\n            out += ' ';\n            out += to_string(r);\n        }\n        out += '\\n';\n    }\n    cout << out;\n    return 0;\n}\n```",
